# Claude Code, always on

An always-on Claude Code agent in a rootless Podman container on Red Hat UBI 9,
which root reaches from a terminal. `ansible/` builds and deploys it with
aslib.infra (see [ansible/README.md](ansible/README.md)).

`config/` is yours. The `Containerfile`, `.containerignore` and this README are
aslib.infra's: `ansible/update-playbooks.yml` replaces them, keeping a changed
one as `<file>.bak` to merge from.

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| `Containerfile` | The image: UBI 9, the tools Claude needs, and Claude Code from Anthropic's signed dnf repository |
| `config/` | Claude Code's `/etc/claude-code/`, mounted read-only, never in the image: `managed-settings.json`, the policy Claude Code reads as an organisation's, above every other setting; `CLAUDE.md`, the instructions it reads in every session (a template: make it yours) |
| `.containerignore` | What never goes into the image build |
| `ansible/` | Building, deploying and entering it on servers, with aslib.infra |

## Without aslib.infra

The image builds and runs with plain Podman 4.3 or newer, as any account:

```sh
podman build --tag claude-code .
mkdir -p ~/claude-code && cp -r config ~/claude-code/
podman run --detach --name claude-code --userns=keep-id:uid=1001,gid=1001 \
  --volume ~/claude-code:/opt/claude-code:Z --volume ~/claude-code/config:/opt/claude-code/config:ro,Z claude-code
podman exec --interactive --tty claude-code claude
```

`~/claude-code` is the container's home, `/opt/claude-code`: Claude keeps its
login, history and memory there. Its `config/` is `/etc/claude-code/`, read-only
for Claude. The container's user (1001) is your account inside it, so what
Claude writes is yours.

## Signing in

The first session asks you to sign in. The browser cannot reach the container,
so the sign-in page shows a code: paste it into Claude. If pasting misbehaves,
run `claude auth login` in a shell in the container (`podman exec -it claude-code
bash`), which reads the code from plain input. The login stays in the
container's home and survives new images.

## The policy

`config/managed-settings.json` makes Claude's home and the shared zone of
aslib.infra's services (`/opt/containers/shared`) its working directories, and
keeps it away from its own login and config (`.claude/`), from `.env` files, and
from the files that would run code at its next start (hooks, `.mcp.json`,
`.git/config`). It may read the rest of the container, which holds only the
read-only image. Its memory goes to
`/opt/claude-code/memory`, its plans to `plans/` in the directory a session
starts in. Its keys are documented in
[Claude Code's settings reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings-reference).

To let Claude's shell commands reach only an allowlist of hosts, add this block
and `bubblewrap socat` to the Containerfile's tools (if Red Hat's UBI repositories
offer them), then build again:

```json
"sandbox": {
  "enabled": true,
  "enableWeakerNestedSandbox": true,
  "failIfUnavailable": true,
  "allowUnsandboxedCommands": false,
  "network": {
    "allowedDomains": ["api.anthropic.com", "claude.ai", "claude.com", "platform.claude.com"],
    "strictAllowlist": true
  }
}
```

It covers shell commands and what they start, not Claude Code's own traffic, and
it needs the weaker nested sandbox inside an unprivileged container.

## Updating Claude Code

Without a pinned version, every build installs the newest Claude Code of the
repository's channel (stable by default): a new image is the update. Claude Code
never updates itself here.
